 create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":458691},{"id":"task-1773259919191-mijisss74","prompt":"when pasting an image into the task windows, we should store these pngs in our claudia cache folder.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-11T20:11:59.289Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T04:45:02.805Z","sessionId":"4cd9fb57-502c-4a1c-9bc4-b44858797fa5","gitState":{"commitBefore":"4b76ee7ce516c962361e3f9ba6297470f06bff32","commitAfter":"4b76ee7ce516c962361e3f9ba6297470f06bff32","uncommittedBefore":true,"filesModified":["github/workflows/tests.yml","backend/src/claudia-mcp-server.ts","backend/src/server.ts","backend/src/task-spawner.ts","frontend/src/App.tsx","frontend/src/__tests__/taskStore.test.ts","frontend/src/components/ConversationHistory.tsx","frontend/src/components/TaskInputBar.tsx","frontend/src/components/WorkspacePanel.tsx","frontend/src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts","frontend/src/stores/taskStore.ts","docs/feature-brainstorm.md","vitest.workspace.ts"],"canRevert":true},"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":586601},{"id":"task-1773253223752-6hlpse7f1","prompt":"Analyze the Claudia codebase for test gaps and testing improvements. Look through the entire project structure. Focus on:\n\n1. **Existing test coverage** - Find all existing test files and understand what's currently tested\n2. **Critical untested paths** - Identify the most important code paths that lack tests, especially:\n   - Task lifecycle (creation, running, completion, failure, cancellation)\n   - WebSocket connection handling and message protocols\n   - PTY spawning and output streaming\n   - API endpoint validation and error responses\n   - Frontend component behavior\n3. **Integration test gaps** - Are there end-to-end tests? What scenarios are missing?\n4. **Test infrastructure** - What testing frameworks are set up? What's missing?\n5. **Testability issues** - Code that's hard to test due to tight coupling, global state, or side effects\n6. **Recommended test plan** - Prioritized list of tests to add, with the highest-impact tests first\n\nFor each gap, provide:\n- What should be tested\n- Why it matters (what could break)\n- Suggested test approach\n- Priority (P0/P1/P2)\n\nDo NOT make any code changes. This is a research-only task.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-11T18:20:23.852Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T22:33:51.031Z","sessionId":"631cd065-0ed3-4657-a504-84a8c668ab33","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":104642},{"id":"task-1773253217154-zxegseomu","prompt":"Analyze the Claudia codebase for bugs and potential issues. Look through both the backend (backend/src/) and frontend (frontend/src/) code. Focus on:\n\n1. **Race conditions** - especially around task spawning, PTY management, and WebSocket connections\n2. **Error handling gaps** - places where errors are swallowed, uncaught promises, or missing try/catch blocks\n3. **Memory leaks** - event listeners not cleaned up, streams not closed, PTY processes not properly terminated\n4. **State management issues** - in both backend (task lifecycle) and frontend (React state)\n5. **Edge cases** - what happens when tasks fail, connections drop, or the server restarts\n6. **Security concerns** - any injection risks, path traversal, or unsafe input handling\n7. **Type safety issues** - any `any` types, unsafe casts, or missing null checks\n\nFor each bug found, provide:\n- File and line number\n- Description of the issue\n- Severity (critical/high/medium/low)\n- Suggested fix\n\nDo NOT make any code changes. This is a research-only task.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-11T18:20:17.255Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T22:34:02.210Z","sessionId":"38e9f18b-6960-4d05-96a6-fa7a182ca4be","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":81784},{"id":"task-1773167210814-75spfvmk5","prompt":"help me diagnose why claude code is not connecting the to the claudia mcp server","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-10T18:26:51.074Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T22:34:11.288Z","sessionId":"6663d493-4253-4eda-bae4-89005995c72a","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":95030},{"id":"task-1773253232465-i4ufarty2","prompt":"Analyze the Claudia codebase to identify new core capabilities and features that would make Claudia more powerful and useful. Claudia is an orchestrator for Claude Code agents - it spawns and manages multiple Claude Code instances via PTY. \n\nResearch the codebase thoroughly, then brainstorm:\n\n1. **Agent Collaboration** - How could agents work together better? Think about:\n   - Shared context/memory between agents\n   - Agent-to-agent communication patterns (beyond what's already built)\n   - Hierarchical task decomposition (parent tasks spawning subtasks)\n   - Consensus/voting mechanisms for code review\n\n2. **Workflow Automation** - What workflows could Claudia automate?\n   - CI/CD integration (react to GitHub events, PR reviews)\n   - Scheduled/cron-based tasks\n   - Event-driven pipelines (file changes trigger agents)\n   - Template-based task patterns\n\n3. **Intelligence Layer** - What smart features could be added?\n   - Task priority and resource management\n   - Learning from past task outcomes\n   - Smart routing (matching tasks to optimal agent configurations)\n   - Cost tracking and optimization\n\n4. **Developer Experience** - What would make Claudia more useful day-to-day?\n   - Better visualization of agent work\n   - Task templates and presets\n   - Integration with IDEs\n   - CLI improvements\n\n5. **Reliability & Scale** - What's needed for production use?\n   - Task persistence and recovery\n   - Multi-machine orchestration\n   - Rate limiting and quota management\n\nFor each capability, provide:\n- Description of the feature\n- Why it's valuable\n- Implementation complexity (low/medium/high)\n- Dependencies or prerequisites\n- How it fits with the existing architecture\n\nDo NOT make any code changes. This is a research-only task.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-11T18:20:32.571Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T22:34:18.211Z","sessionId":"31a0ea64-d7ac-4550-b02b-e6d4767cb92d","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":46683},{"id":"task-1773272805794-2ybnb8c0f","prompt":"can you fix and remove the \"sending query to...\", it's not necessary to indicate this for every message since it's obvious. \n\n[Attached image: C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia\\backend\\uploads\\image-1773272804916-972005149.png]","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4","createdAt":"2026-03-11T23:46:45.911Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T22:44:26.666Z","sessionId":"b89109d4-b551-4a11-87e4-c34b4c4987cd","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":132889},{"id":"task-1773257443465-mcb6ast07","prompt":"what branch are we on?","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6","createdAt":"2026-03-11T19:30:43.576Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-13T02:08:42.382Z","sessionId":"e031f23a-e2e3-4b59-9949-57966102c4cf","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":4155757,"displayName":"fix links"},{"id":"task-1773261441789-r13qza6d1","prompt":"when i drag and move different tasks, they somehow reset to their original positions after some time or event","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-11T20:37:21.935Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-13T02:50:20.758Z","sessionId":"625aa592-e894-42c0-ac2a-eb5e748d7dc3","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":2844386},{"id":"task-1773356897690-g68v605uy","prompt":"when i control+v in the claude code terminal, it pastes twice.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\claudia","createdAt":"2026-03-12T23:08:17.921Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-13T02:50:23.747Z","sessionId":"efe7dfcd-5a83-4c44-943d-15d3584341e2","gitState":{"commitBefore":"778d7f00d0e2cfdd878734d2acb44d7337a3b85d","commitAfter":"bbea804a80b3296b2dfc9d793301c9ae7f3cab0d","uncommittedBefore":true,"filesModified":["frontend/src/components/ShellTerminalView.tsx","frontend/src/components/TerminalView.tsx","docs/feature-brainstorm.md","vitest.workspace.ts"],"canRevert":false},"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing","historySize":546160},{"id":"task-1773257590954-sonlniqwj","prompt":"b","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia7","createdAt":"2026-03-11T19:33:11.056Z","las