ntly\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing","historySize":0},{"id":"task-1773100983842-g4tqs03w7","prompt":"analyze the gaia repo to create an agent that can help find deals and track prices similar to https://camelcamelcamel.com/.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia3","createdAt":"2026-03-10T00:03:04.285Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-14T02:45:59.863Z","sessionId":"d9f553a9-f852-43f2-8d66-a2e761096ffb","historySize":16106},{"id":"task-1773256462518-lwwr3hc1q","prompt":"I'm having issues with the installation scripts in gaia, can you investigate? also it seems like it installed the older version, we are on v0.16.0:\nPS C:\\Users\\14255> irm https://amd-gaia.ai/install.ps1 | iex\n﻿# : The term '﻿#' is not recognized as the name of a cmdlet, function, script file, or operable\nprogram. Check the spelling of the name, or if a path was included, verify that the path is\ncorrect and try again.\nAt line:1 char:1\n+ ﻿# GAIA Installer for Windows\n+ ~~\n    + CategoryInfo          : ObjectNotFound: (﻿#:String) [], CommandNotFoundException\n    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : CommandNotFoundException\n\n\n\n========================================\n  GAIA Installer for Windows\n========================================\n\n\n[*] Checking for uv package manager...\n[✓] uv is already installed\nTrue\n[!] GAIA is already installed at C:\\Users\\14255\\.gaia\n[*] Checking for updates...\nC:\\Users\\14255\\.gaia\\venv\\Scripts\\python.exe: No module named pip\n[✓] GAIA updated to latest version\n[*] Adding GAIA to PATH...\n[✓] GAIA is already in PATH\n\n================================\n  GAIA Installed Successfully!\n================================\n\n\nNext steps:\n  1. Close and reopen your terminal (or run: refreshenv)\n  2. Run: gaia init to set up Lemonade Server and download models\n  3. Start chatting: gaia chat\n\n\nDocumentation: https://amd-gaia.ai\nIssues: https://github.com/amd/gaia/issues\n\n\nPS C:\\Users\\14255> gaia --version\n0.15.3.1","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia3","createdAt":"2026-03-11T19:14:22.620Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-12T05:44:19.254Z","sessionId":"93657f0a-35ab-4dc5-bcba-25a2730676b6","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.","historySize":0},{"id":"task-1773457014735-ntnh0cwnu","prompt":"## Task: Add GAIA UI Initialization Frontend\n\nYou need to implement the frontend for a new \"first-run initialization\" feature in the GAIA Agent UI. When the app starts for the first time (not yet initialized), it shows a full-screen initialization screen with an \"Initialize\" button and a \"Skip\" option.\n\n### IMPORTANT RULES\n- Use complete absolute Windows paths with drive letters for ALL file operations (e.g., `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\...`)\n- Do NOT commit anything\n- Do NOT touch port 4001\n- Do NOT modify any Python backend files (anything in `src/gaia/ui/` or `src/gaia/installer/` etc.)\n- Only modify files in `src/gaia/apps/webui/src/`\n\n### API Contract (already implemented by backend)\n\nThe backend provides these endpoints:\n\n```\nGET /api/init/status → { initialized: boolean }\nPOST /api/init/skip → { initialized: true }\nPOST /api/init/reset → { initialized: false }\nPOST /api/init/start → SSE stream with events:\n  data: {\"type\": \"log\", \"content\": \"...\"}\n  data: {\"type\": \"progress\", \"step\": 1, \"total\": 4, \"message\": \"Checking Lemonade Server...\"}\n  data: {\"type\": \"done\", \"success\": true}\n  data: {\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": \"...\"}\n```\n\n### Changes Required\n\n#### 1. Add API functions\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\apps\\webui\\src\\services\\api.ts`**\n\nAdd these functions at the end of the file (before the closing, after the schedule functions):\n\n```typescript\n// -- Initialization -----------------------------------------------------------\n\nexport async function getInitStatus(): Promise<{ initialized: boolean }> {\n    return apiFetch('GET', '/init/status');\n}\n\nexport async function skipInit(): Promise<{ initialized: boolean }> {\n    return apiFetch('POST', '/init/skip');\n}\n\nexport async function resetInit(): Promise<{ initialized: boolean }> {\n    return apiFetch('POST', '/init/reset');\n}\n\nexport interface InitStreamCallbacks {\n    onLog: (content: string) => void;\n    onProgress: (step: number, total: number, message: string) => void;\n    onDone: (success: boolean) => void;\n    onError: (message: string) => void;\n}\n\nexport function startInit(callbacks: InitStreamCallbacks): AbortController {\n    const controller = new AbortController();\n\n    fetch(`${API_BASE}/init/start`, {\n        method: 'POST',\n        signal: controller.signal,\n    })\n        .then(async (res) => {\n            if (!res.ok) {\n                const errText = await res.text().catch(() => '');\n                callbacks.onError(`HTTP ${res.status}: ${errText}`);\n                return;\n            }\n\n            const reader = res.body?.getReader();\n            if (!reader) {\n                callbacks.onError('No response body');\n                return;\n            }\n\n            const decoder = new TextDecoder();\n            let buffer = '';\n\n            try {\n                while (true) {\n                    const { done, value } = await reader.read();\n                    if (done) break;\n\n                    buffer += decoder.decode(value, { stream: true });\n                    const lines = buffer.split('\\n');\n                    buffer = lines.pop() || '';\n\n                    for (const line of lines) {\n                        if (line.startsWith('data: ')) {\n                            const raw = line.slice(6).trim();\n                            if (!raw) continue;\n                            try {\n                                const event = JSON.parse(raw);\n                                if (event.type === 'log') {\n                                    callbacks.onLog(event.content || '');\n                                } else if (event.type === 'progress') {\n                                    callbacks.onProgress(event.step, event.total, event.message || '');\n                                } else if (event.type === 'done') {\n                                    callbacks.onDone(event.success ?? false);\n                                } else if (event.type === 'error') {\n                                    callbacks.onError(event.message || 'Unknown error');\n                                }\n                            } catch {\n                                // Skip malformed SSE data\n                            }\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            } finally {\n                reader.releaseLock();\n            }\n        })\n        .catch((err) => {\n            if (err.name !== 'AbortError') {\n                callbacks.onError(err.message || 'Connection failed');\n            }\n        });\n\n    return controller;\n}\n```\n\n#### 2. Create InitScreen Component\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\apps\\webui\\src\\components\\InitScreen.tsx`** (NEW FILE)\n\n```tsx\n// Copyright(C) 2025-2026 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\nimport { useState, useRef, useEffect, useCallback } from 'react';\nimport { Download, SkipForward, CheckCircle, XCircle, Loader2, RotateCcw } from 'lucide-react';\nimport * as api from '../services/api';\nimport './InitScreen.css';\n\ninterface InitScreenProps {\n    onComplete: () => void;\n}\n\ntype InitState = 'idle' | 'running' | 'success' | 'error';\n\nexport function InitScreen({ onComplete }: InitScreenProps) {\n    const [state, setState] = useState<InitState>('idle');\n    const [logs, setLogs] = useState<string[]>([]);\n    const [currentStep, setCurrentStep] = useState(0);\n    const [totalSteps, setTotalSteps] = useState(4);\n    const [stepMessage, setStepMessage] = useState('');\n    const [errorMessage, setErrorMessage] = useState('');\n    const logEndRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);\n    const controllerRef = useRef<AbortController | null>(null);\n\n    // Auto-scroll log to bottom\n    useEffect(() => {\n        logEndRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth' });\n    }, [logs]);\n\n    const handleInitialize = useCallback(() => {\n        setState('running');\n        setLogs([]);\n        setCurrentStep(0);\n        setErrorMessage('');\n\n        controllerRef.current = api.startInit({\n            onLog: (content) => {\n                setLogs(prev => [...prev, content]);\n            },\n            onProgress: (step, total, message) => {\n                setCurrentStep(step);\n                setTotalSteps(total);\n                setStepMessage(message);\n            },\n            onDone: (success) => {\n                if (success) {\n                    setState('success');\n                } else {\n                    setState('error');\n                }\n            },\n            onError: (message) => {\n                setErrorMessage(message);\n                setLogs(prev => [...prev, `Error: ${message}`]);\n            },\n        });\n    }, []);\n\n    const handleSkip = useCallback(async () => {\n        try {\n            await api.skipInit();\n            onComplete();\n        } catch (err) {\n            console.error('Failed to skip init:', err);\n            // Still proceed even if skip API fails\n            onComplete();\n        }\n    }, [onComplete]);\n\n    const handleRetry = useCallback(() => {\n        setState('idle');\n        setLogs([]);\n        setCurrentStep(0);\n        setStepMessage('');\n        setErrorMessage('');\n    }, []);\n\n    const handleContinue = useCallback(() => {\n        onComplete();\n    }, [onComplete]);\n\n    // Cleanup on unmount\n    useEffect(() => {\n        return () => {\n            controllerRef.current?.abort();\n        };\n    }, []);\n\n    return (\n        <div className=\"init-screen\">\n            <div className=\"init-container\">\n                {state === 'idle' && (\n                    <div className=\"init-welcome\">\n                        <h1 className=\"init-title\">Welcome to GAIA</h1>\n                        <p className=\"init-subtitle\">\n                            Your private AI assistant, running 100% locally on AMD Ryzen AI\n                        </p>\n                        <p className=\"init-description\">\n                            GAIA needs to download AI models before you can start chatting.\n                            This is a one-time setup that typically takes a few minutes.\n                        </p>\n\n                        <div className=\"init-actions\">\n                            <button className=\"btn-primary init-btn\" onClick={handleInitialize}>\n                                <Download size={18} />\n                                Initialize GAIA\n                            </button>\n                            <button className=\"btn-ghost init-skip-btn\" onClick={handleSkip}>\n                                <SkipForward size={16} />\n                                Skip for now\n                            </button>\n                        </div>\n\n                        <p className=\"init-hint\">\n                            You can also run <code>gaia init ui</code> from the command line\n                        </p>\n                    </div>\n                )}\n\n                {state === 'running' && (\n                    <div className=\"init-progress\">\n                        <h2 className=\"init-progress-title\">\n                            <Loader2 size={22} className=\"init-spinner\" />\n                            Initializing GAIA\n                        </h2>\n\n                        {currentStep > 0 && (\n                            <div className=\"init-step-info\">\n                                <div className=\"init-step-bar\">\n                                    <div\n                                        className=\"init-step-fill\"\n                                        style={{ width: `${(currentStep / totalSteps) * 100}%` }}\n                                    />\n                                </div>\n                                <span className=\"init-step-label\">\n                                    Step {currentStep}/{totalSteps}: {stepMessage}\n                                </span>\n                            </div>\n                        )}\n\n                        <div className=\"init-log\">\n                            {logs.map((line, i) => (\n                                <div key={i} className={`init-log-line ${line.startsWith('   ✓') ? 'success' : line.startsWith('   ❌') || line.startsWith('Error:') ? 'error' : line.startsWith('   ⚠') ? 'warning' : ''}`}>\n                                    {line}\n                                </div>\n                            ))}\n                            <div ref={logEndRef} />\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                )}\n\n                {state === 'success' && (\n                    <div className=\"init-result\">\n                        <CheckCircle size={48} className=\"init-success-icon\" />\n                        <h2>GAIA is Ready!</h2>\n                        <p>All models have been downloaded and verified successfully.</p>\n                        <button className=\"btn-primary init-btn\" onClick={handleContinue}>\n                            Get Started\n                        </button>\n                    </div>\n                )}\n\n                {state === 'error' && (\n                    <div className=\"init-result\">\n                        <XCircle size={48} className=\"init-error-icon\" />\n                        <h2>Initialization Failed</h2>\n                        <p className=\"init-error-msg\">{errorMessage || 'An error occurred during initialization.'}</p>\n\n                        <div className=\"init-log init-log-error\">\n                            {logs.slice(-20).map((line, i) => (\n                                <div key={i} className={`init-log-line ${line.startsWith('   ✓') ? 'success' : line.startsWith('   ❌') || line.startsWith('Error:') ? 'error' : ''}`}>\n                                    {line}\n                                </div>\n                            ))}\n                            <div ref={logEndRef} />\n                        </div>\n\n                        <div className=\"init-actions\">\n                            <button className=\"btn-primary init-btn\" onClick={handleRetry}>\n                                <RotateCcw size={16} />\n                                Try Again\n                            </button>\n                            <button className=\"btn-ghost init-skip-btn\" onClick={handleSkip}>\n                                <SkipForward size={16} />\n                                Skip for now\n                            </button>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                )}\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    );\n}\n```\n\n#### 3. Create InitScreen CSS\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\apps\\webui\\src\\components\\InitScreen.css`** (NEW FILE)\n\n```css\n/* Init Screen - Full-screen initialization overlay */\n\n.init-screen {\n    position: fixed;\n    inset: 0;\n    z-index: 1000;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    background: var(--bg-primary);\n    padding: 24px;\n}\n\n.init-container {\n    max-width: 640px;\n    width: 100%;\n}\n\n/* ── Welcome State ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n.init-welcome {\n    text-align: center;\n}\n\n.init-title {\n    font-size: 42px;\n    font-weight: 800;\n    letter-spacing: -0.5px;\n    background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--amd-red), var(--amd-red-light));\n    -webkit-background-clip: text;\n    -webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;\n    background-clip: text;\n    margin-bottom: 12px;\n}\n\n.init-subtitle {\n    font-size: 16px;\n    color: var(--text-secondary);\n    margin-bottom: 24px;\n    line-height: 1.5;\n}\n\n.init-description {\n    font-size: 14px;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    margin-bottom: 32px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n    max-width: 480px;\n    margin-left: auto;\n    margin-right: auto;\n}\n\n.init-actions {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 12px;\n    margin-bottom: 24px;\n}\n\n.init-btn {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 8px;\n    padding: 12px 32px;\n    font-size: 15px;\n}\n\n.init-skip-btn {\n    display: inline-flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 6px;\n    padding: 8px 20px;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n    background: transparent;\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n    cursor: pointer;\n    transition: all var(--duration) var(--ease);\n}\n\n.init-skip-btn:hover {\n    color: var(--text-secondary);\n    border-color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n.init-hint {\n    font-size: 12px;\n    color: var(--text-muted);\n}\n\n.init-hint code {\n    background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    padding: 2px 6px;\n    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'Fira Code', 'Cascadia Code', monospace);\n}\n\n/* ── Progress State ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n.init-progress {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 16px;\n}\n\n.init-progress-title {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 10px;\n    font-size: 20px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n}\n\n.init-spinner {\n    animation: spin 1s linear infinite;\n    color: var(--amd-red);\n}\n\n@keyframes spin {\n    to { transform: rotate(360deg); }\n}\n\n.init-step-info {\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    gap: 6px;\n}\n\n.init-step-bar {\n    height: 6px;\n    background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-full);\n    overflow: hidden;\n}\n\n.init-step-fill {\n    height: 100%;\n    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--amd-red), var(--amd-red-light));\n    border-radius: var(--radius-full);\n    transition: width 0.5s ease;\n}\n\n.init-step-label {\n    font-size: 13px;\n    color: var(--text-secondary);\n}\n\n.init-log {\n    background: var(--bg-secondary);\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    border-radius: var(--radius-md);\n    padding: 16px;\n    max-height: 400px;\n    overflow-y: auto;\n    font-family: var(--font-mono, 'Fira Code', 'Cascadia Code', monospace);\n    font-size: 12px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\n.init-log-error {\n    max-height: 200px;\n    margin-bottom: 16px;\n}\n\n.init-log-line {\n    white-space: pre-wrap;\n    word-break: break-word;\n    color: var(--text-primary);\n}\n\n.init-log-line.success {\n    color: #22c55e;\n}\n\n.init-log-line.error {\n    color: #ef4444;\n}\n\n.init-log-line.warning {\n    color: #f59e0b;\n}\n\n/* ── Result States ──────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n.init-result {\n    text-align: center;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 12px;\n}\n\n.init-success-icon {\n    color: #22c55e;\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.init-error-icon {\n    color: #ef4444;\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.init-result h2 {\n    font-size: 24px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    margin-bottom: 4px;\n}\n\n.init-result p {\n    font-size: 14px;\n    color: var(--text-secondary);\n    max-width: 400px;\n}\n\n.init-error-msg {\n    color: var(--text-muted) !important;\n    font-size: 13px !important;\n}\n\n/* ── Responsive ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n@media (max-width: 768px) {\n    .init-screen {\n        padding: 16px;\n    }\n\n    .init-title {\n        font-size: 32px;\n    }\n\n    .init-log {\n        max-height: 300px;\n        font-size: 11px;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n#### 4. Update App.tsx to show InitScreen\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\apps\\webui\\src\\App.tsx`**\n\nMake these specific changes:\n\na) Add the InitScreen import at the top (with other component imports, around line 8):\n```typescript\nimport { InitScreen } from './components/InitScreen';\n```\n\nb) Add state for initialization tracking inside the App function (around line 37, after the tunnel state):\n```typescript\n// Initialization state\nconst [initialized, setInitialized] = useState<boolean | null>(null); // null = loading\n```\n\nc) Add a useEffect to check init status on mount (add after the tunnel status check useEffect, around line 144):\n```typescript\n// Check initialization status on mount\nuseEffect(() => {\n    api.getInitStatus()\n        .then((status) => {\n            setInitialized(status.initialized);\n        })\n        .catch(() => {\n            // If we can't check, assume initialized (don't block the app)\n            setInitialized(true);\n        });\n}, []);\n```\n\nd) In the JSX return, wrap the entire app content with an initialization check. Replace the return statement (starting around line 250) with:\n\n```tsx\n// Show loading while checking init status\nif (initialized === null) {\n    return null; // Brief flash while checking - could add a spinner\n}\n\n// Show init screen if not initialized\nif (initialized === false) {\n    return <InitScreen onComplete={() => setInitialized(true)} />;\n}\n\nreturn (\n    <div className=\"app\">\n        {/* ... existing JSX stays exactly the same ... */}\n    </div>\n);\n```\n\nIMPORTANT: Keep ALL the existing JSX inside the final `return (...)` exactly as it is. Only add the two early returns before it.\n\n### Verification\n\nAfter making all changes:\n1. Re-read each modified file to verify correctness\n2. Make sure all imports are present and correct\n3. Verify the InitScreen component handles all states (idle, running, success, error)\n4. Verify the API functions match the contract described above\n5. Verify App.tsx correctly gates the main UI behind initialization check\n\nDo NOT run any build commands or tests. Just make the code changes and verify them by re-reading the files.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6","createdAt":"2026-03-14T02:56:54.978Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-14T09:58:00.012Z","sessionId":"51c66523-08cd-4cf3-8e93-fbb5d4ba3e41","gitState":{"commitBefore":"8a530fc1910d1289c681045c0c2ae7e7ff75a9dd","commitAfter":"b4cefa6c58e8369b19ff624ec3cebd81dea52837","uncommittedBefore":true,"filesModified":["CLAUDE.md","docs/guides/agent-ui.mdx","docs/reference/cli.mdx","docs/spec/agent-ui-server.mdx","docs/spec/tray-app-integration.md","scripts/build-ui-installer.ps1","scripts/build-ui-installer.sh","src/gaia/agents/base/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/base/errors.py","src/gaia/agents/routing/agent.py","src/gaia/apps/webui/app.config.json","src/gaia/apps/webui/bin/gaia-ui.mjs","src/gaia/apps/webui/main.cjs","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/App.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/ChatView.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/ConnectionBanner.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/SettingsModal.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/SettingsModal.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/services/api.ts","src/gaia/cli.py","src/gaia/installer/init_command.py","src/gaia/llm/lemonade_client.py","src/gaia/llm/vlm_client.py","src/gaia/rag/sdk.py","src/gaia/ui/_chat_helpers.py","src/gaia/ui/routers/init.py","src/gaia/ui/server.py","tests/integration/test_chat_ui_integration.py","tests/unit/test_init_router.py","etup.py","src/gaia/agents/chat/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/chat/app.py","src/gaia/agents/code/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/docker/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/emr/cli.py","src/gaia/agents/emr/dashboard/server.py","src/gaia/agents/jira/agent.py","src/gaia/apps/jira/app.py","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/Sidebar.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/Sidebar.tsx","src/gaia/eval/fix_code_testbench/fix_code_testbench.py","src/gaia/mcp/mcp_bridge.py","src/gaia/mcp/servers/docker_mcp.py","src/gaia/ui/database.py",".claude/scheduled_tasks.lock",".playwright-mcp/","src/gaia/config.py","v17.md"],"canRevert":false},"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\nYou have access to the following reference directories. Use them as examples or context when relevant to the task. You can read files from these directories using their absolute paths.\n\n## Reference: \"gaia4\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia5\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia5)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia)\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing","historySize":2049250,"displayName":"Init Screen: Frontend"},{"id":"task-1773456951421-53gyxxav3","prompt":"## Task: Add GAIA UI Initialization Backend\n\nYou need to implement the backend for a new \"first-run initialization\" feature in the GAIA Agent UI. This feature shows an initialization screen when the UI starts for the first time, allowing users to download required LLMs.\n\n### Overview\n\nThe Agent UI already has an `initialized` marker file at `~/.gaia/chat/initialized` that is checked in `src/gaia/ui/routers/system.py` (lines 97-98). We need to:\n\n1. Add a new \"ui\" profile to the initialization system\n2. Create a new FastAPI router for initialization endpoints\n3. Register the router in the server\n\n### IMPORTANT RULES\n- Use complete absolute Windows paths with drive letters for ALL file operations (e.g., `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\...`)\n- Use forward slashes in import paths\n- Do NOT commit anything\n- Do NOT touch port 4001\n- NEVER modify frontend files (anything in `src/gaia/apps/webui/`)\n\n### Changes Required\n\n#### 1. Add \"ui\" profile to INIT_PROFILES\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\installer\\init_command.py`**\n\nAdd a \"ui\" entry to the `INIT_PROFILES` dict (around line 39-100). Place it before the \"all\" entry:\n\n```python\n\"ui\": {\n    \"description\": \"Agent UI with chat, RAG, and vision support\",\n    \"agent\": \"ui\",\n    \"models\": None,  # Use agent profile defaults\n    \"approx_size\": \"~25 GB\",\n    \"min_lemonade_version\": \"9.0.4\",\n    \"min_context_size\": 32768,\n},\n```\n\n#### 2. Add \"ui\" agent profile to AGENT_PROFILES\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\llm\\lemonade_client.py`**\n\nAdd a \"ui\" entry to the `AGENT_PROFILES` dict (around line 182-253). Place it after the \"chat\" entry:\n\n```python\n\"ui\": AgentProfile(\n    name=\"ui\",\n    display_name=\"Agent UI\",\n    models=[\"qwen3.5-35b\", \"nomic-embed\"],\n    min_ctx_size=32768,\n    description=\"Agent UI with chat and RAG support\",\n),\n```\n\n#### 3. Add \"ui\" to agent_context_sizes in cli.py\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\cli.py`**\n\nFind the `agent_context_sizes` dict (around line 145-160) and add:\n```python\n\"ui\": 32768,\n```\n\n#### 4. Create initialization router\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\ui\\routers\\init.py`** (NEW FILE)\n\nCreate a new router with these endpoints:\n\n```python\n# Copyright(C) 2025-2026 Advanced Micro Devices, Inc. All rights reserved.\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n\"\"\"Initialization endpoints for GAIA Agent UI first-run setup.\"\"\"\n\nimport asyncio\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter\nfrom fastapi.responses import JSONResponse, StreamingResponse\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(__name__)\n\nrouter = APIRouter(tags=[\"init\"])\n\n# Marker file path\nINIT_MARKER = Path.home() / \".gaia\" / \"chat\" / \"initialized\"\n\n\n@router.get(\"/api/init/status\")\nasync def init_status():\n    \"\"\"Check whether first-run initialization has been completed.\"\"\"\n    return {\"initialized\": INIT_MARKER.exists()}\n\n\n@router.post(\"/api/init/skip\")\nasync def init_skip():\n    \"\"\"Skip initialization and mark as initialized.\"\"\"\n    INIT_MARKER.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    INIT_MARKER.write_text(\"skipped\")\n    logger.info(\"Initialization skipped by user\")\n    return {\"initialized\": True}\n\n\n@router.post(\"/api/init/reset\")\nasync def init_reset():\n    \"\"\"Reset initialization state (for re-initialization).\"\"\"\n    if INIT_MARKER.exists():\n        INIT_MARKER.unlink()\n        logger.info(\"Initialization state reset\")\n    return {\"initialized\": False}\n\n\n@router.post(\"/api/init/start\")\nasync def init_start():\n    \"\"\"Start GAIA initialization with the 'ui' profile.\n    \n    Runs `gaia init ui --yes` as a subprocess and streams stdout/stderr\n    as Server-Sent Events so the frontend can display real-time progress.\n    \n    SSE event types:\n    - log: A line of output from the init process\n    - progress: Step progress update (step, total, message)\n    - done: Initialization complete (success: bool)\n    - error: An error occurred (message: str)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    async def event_stream():\n        \"\"\"Generate SSE events from the init subprocess.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            # Run gaia init with the ui profile\n            cmd = [sys.executable, \"-m\", \"gaia.cli\", \"init\", \"ui\", \"--yes\"]\n            logger.info(\"Starting initialization: %s\", \" \".join(cmd))\n\n            # Start subprocess with line-buffered output\n            process = await asyncio.create_subprocess_exec(\n                *cmd,\n                stdout=asyncio.subprocess.PIPE,\n                stderr=asyncio.subprocess.STDOUT,\n                env=None,  # inherit environment\n            )\n\n            step_num = 0\n            total_steps = 4\n\n            # Stream output line by line\n            while True:\n                line = await process.stdout.readline()\n                if not line:\n                    break\n\n                text = line.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\").rstrip()\n                if not text:\n                    continue\n\n                logger.debug(\"Init output: %s\", text)\n\n                # Detect step progress from output\n                if text.startswith(\"Step \"):\n                    try:\n                        parts = text.split(\":\")\n                        step_part = parts[0].strip()  # \"Step X/Y\"\n                        msg_part = \":\".join(parts[1:]).strip()\n                        nums = step_part.replace(\"Step \", \"\").split(\"/\")\n                        step_num = int(nums[0])\n                        total_steps = int(nums[1])\n                        event = {\n                            \"type\": \"progress\",\n                            \"step\": step_num,\n                            \"total\": total_steps,\n                            \"message\": msg_part,\n                        }\n                        yield f\"data: {json.dumps(event)}\\n\\n\"\n                    except (ValueError, IndexError):\n                        pass\n\n                # Send every line as a log event\n                event = {\"type\": \"log\", \"content\": text}\n                yield f\"data: {json.dumps(event)}\\n\\n\"\n\n            # Wait for process to finish\n            return_code = await process.wait()\n            logger.info(\"Initialization process exited with code %d\", return_code)\n\n            if return_code == 0:\n                # Mark as initialized\n                INIT_MARKER.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n                INIT_MARKER.write_text(\"initialized\")\n                logger.info(\"Initialization completed successfully\")\n                yield f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"done\", \"success\": True})}\\n\\n'\n            else:\n                error_msg = f\"Initialization failed with exit code {return_code}\"\n                logger.error(error_msg)\n                yield f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": error_msg})}\\n\\n'\n                yield f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"done\", \"success\": False})}\\n\\n'\n\n        except Exception as e:\n            error_msg = f\"Initialization error: {str(e)}\"\n            logger.exception(error_msg)\n            yield f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"error\", \"message\": error_msg})}\\n\\n'\n            yield f'data: {json.dumps({\"type\": \"done\", \"success\": False})}\\n\\n'\n\n    return StreamingResponse(\n        event_stream(),\n        media_type=\"text/event-stream\",\n        headers={\n            \"Cache-Control\": \"no-cache\",\n            \"Connection\": \"keep-alive\",\n            \"X-Accel-Buffering\": \"no\",\n        },\n    )\n```\n\n#### 5. Register the init router in server.py\n\n**File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6\\src\\gaia\\ui\\server.py`**\n\nAdd the import (around line 48-54, with other router imports):\n```python\nfrom .routers import init as init_router_mod\n```\n\nAdd the router registration (around line 246-252, with other router includes):\n```python\napp.include_router(init_router_mod.router)\n```\n\n### Verification\n\nAfter making all changes:\n1. Re-read each modified file to verify correctness\n2. Make sure all imports are correct\n3. Make sure the init router SSE format matches what I described\n4. Check that the \"ui\" profile is valid and referenced correctly\n\nDo NOT run any tests or build commands. Just make the code changes and verify them by re-reading the files.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6","createdAt":"2026-03-14T02:55:51.681Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-14T10:13:15.399Z","sessionId":"7b64c02e-1df2-4f3c-9192-1db38fa5fef7","gitState":{"commitBefore":"8a530fc1910d1289c681045c0c2ae7e7ff75a9dd","commitAfter":"b4cefa6c58e8369b19ff624ec3cebd81dea52837","uncommittedBefore":true,"filesModified":["CLAUDE.md","docs/guides/agent-ui.mdx","docs/reference/cli.mdx","docs/spec/agent-ui-server.mdx","docs/spec/tray-app-integration.md","scripts/build-ui-installer.ps1","scripts/build-ui-installer.sh","src/gaia/agents/base/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/base/errors.py","src/gaia/agents/routing/agent.py","src/gaia/apps/webui/app.config.json","src/gaia/apps/webui/bin/gaia-ui.mjs","src/gaia/apps/webui/main.cjs","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/App.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/ChatView.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/ConnectionBanner.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/SettingsModal.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/SettingsModal.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/services/api.ts","src/gaia/cli.py","src/gaia/installer/init_command.py","src/gaia/llm/lemonade_client.py","src/gaia/llm/vlm_client.py","src/gaia/rag/sdk.py","src/gaia/ui/_chat_helpers.py","src/gaia/ui/routers/init.py","src/gaia/ui/server.py","tests/integration/test_chat_ui_integration.py","tests/unit/test_init_router.py","rc/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.css",".claude/scheduled_tasks.lock",".playwright-mcp/","v17.md"],"canRevert":false},"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\nYou have access to the following reference directories. Use them as examples or context when relevant to the task. You can read files from these directories using their absolute paths.\n\n## Reference: \"gaia4\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia5\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia5)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia)\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing","historySize":4135191,"displayName":"Init Screen: Backend"},{"id":"task-1773456891993-aqj3g17we","prompt":"when something bad happens such as the following error, lets present a better formatted error with gaia's agent personality, then provide an option (similar to agent tool calls) for the user to expand a window above the message to view the full error.\nUnable to complete task due to error: HTTPConnectionPool(host='localhost', port=8000): Max retries exceeded with url: /api/v1/chat/completions (Caused by NewConnectionError(\"HTTPConnection(host='localhost', port=8000): Failed to establish a new connection: [WinError 10061] No connection could be made because the target machine actively refused it\"))","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia6","createdAt":"2026-03-14T02:54:52.249Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-14T10:13:17.456Z","sessionId":"dc3a278a-a747-4bb1-b351-08db57efade2","gitState":{"commitBefore":"8a530fc1910d1289c681045c0c2ae7e7ff75a9dd","commitAfter":"8a530fc1910d1289c681045c0c2ae7e7ff75a9dd","uncommittedBefore":true,"filesModified":["rc/gaia/agents/base/agent.py","src/gaia/agents/base/errors.py","src/gaia/agents/routing/agent.py","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/App.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/ChatView.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/MessageBubble.tsx","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/services/api.ts","src/gaia/cli.py","src/gaia/installer/init_command.py","src/gaia/llm/lemonade_client.py","src/gaia/llm/vlm_client.py","src/gaia/rag/sdk.py","src/gaia/ui/_chat_helpers.py","src/gaia/ui/server.py","tests/integration/test_chat_ui_integration.py",".claude/scheduled_tasks.lock",".playwright-mcp/","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.css","src/gaia/apps/webui/src/components/InitScreen.tsx","src/gaia/ui/routers/init.py","tests/unit/test_init_router.py","v17.md"],"canRevert":true},"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\nYou have access to the following reference directories. Use them as examples or context when relevant to the task. You can read files from these directories using their absolute paths.\n\n## Reference: \"gaia4\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia5\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia5)\n\n## Reference: \"gaia\" (C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia)\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing","historySize":4145769},{"id":"task-1773456957875-dqpzsfy4s","prompt":"when a model is being downloaded during a query, nothing is presented to the user making it seem like the agent has hung. we should provide information on what's happening, in this case model is being downloaded along with the progress callback: 2026-03-13 19:52:57.394 [Info] (ModelManager) Downloading: Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf...\n  Progress: 100% (0.0/0.0 MB)\n  Progress: 0% (72.5/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 0% (174.7/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 1% (278.9/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 1% (384.3/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 2% (489.4/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 2% (595.3/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 3% (702.5/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 3% (808.4/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 4% (916.0/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 4% (1020.9/21211.6 MB)\n  Progress: 5% (110