r archive completed tasks** — the user wants to review their outputs. After a task completes, just report its status and read its output. Do NOT call `claudia_delete_task` or `claudia_archive_task` on finished tasks.","historySize":0,"displayName":"Eval Batch 5 — 4 Scenarios"},{"id":"task-1774001257056-hpyynkdsc","prompt":"Read C:/Users/14255/Work/gaia4/eval/prompts/batch4_instructions.md and execute all 5 scenarios exactly as specified.","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4","createdAt":"2026-03-20T10:07:37.602Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-20T10:34:05.765Z","sessionId":"5e4c3785-2765-456a-9f8f-0e882085ab27","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Auto-title your task:**\n- Early in your work (after understanding the task), use `claudia_rename_task` to give YOUR OWN task a short, descriptive title (3-6 words) that reflects what you're actually doing\n- Your task ID is provided in the `claudia_rename_task` tool description — use it to rename yourself\n- If the user has manually edited your task title, the rename will be rejected — do NOT retry\n- If your work evolves significantly, update your title to reflect the new focus (unless user-edited)\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing\n- **NEVER delete or archive completed tasks** — the user wants to review their outputs. After a task completes, just report its status and read its output. Do NOT call `claudia_delete_task` or `claudia_archive_task` on finished tasks.","historySize":0,"displayName":"Eval Batch 4 — 5 Scenarios"},{"id":"task-1774005122215-v3frx1c80","prompt":"You are re-running 3 eval scenarios that previously FAILed. Code fixes have just been applied. Your job is to execute each scenario via the gaia-agent-ui MCP tools, score the results, and write updated JSON files.\n\n## CRITICAL RULES\n- NEVER call `delete_session`\n- ALWAYS pass `session_id` to `index_document`\n- Write results to `eval/results/rerun/` (overwrite existing files)\n- Extended thinking spinner names (Razzmatazzing, Unfurling, Philosophising, etc.) are NORMAL — not errors\n- Max 2 fix attempts per turn (Fix Protocol below)\n\n## Fix Protocol\nWhen agent gives wrong/incomplete answer:\n1. **Fix 1 (path failure):** Re-send original question as-is\n2. **Fix 2 (no answer):** \"Please check again — I believe the document has the answer.\"\n3. **Fix 3 (verbose):** \"Please give a shorter answer — 1-2 sentences max.\"\n4. **Fix 4 (context loss):** Re-state context: \"Earlier you found [X]. Based on that, [original question].\"\n5. **Fix 5 (hallucinated fact):** \"Please check the document — I believe that figure may be incorrect.\"\n\n---\n\n## SCENARIO 1: search_empty_fallback\n**File:** `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\prompts\\run_search_empty_fallback.md`\n\nRead that prompt file for full instructions. Key facts:\n- Ground truth: `api_reference.py` in `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\corpus\\documents\\`\n- T1: \"How does the API handle authentication?\" → Bearer token via Authorization header\n- T2: \"What endpoints are available in that API?\" → /v1/chat/completions, /v1/models, /health\n- T3: \"Find documentation about the XYZ authentication protocol.\" → Not found (should NOT fabricate)\n- Previous score: 5.40 FAIL\n- Fix applied: `.py` now included in `search_file` default scope\n- Write result to: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\results\\rerun\\search_empty_fallback.json`\n\nSteps:\n1. `system_status()` — verify Agent UI running\n2. `create_session(\"Eval: search_empty_fallback\")` — DO NOT pre-index anything\n3. Turn 1: send \"How does the API handle authentication? I think there's documentation somewhere.\"\n4. Turn 2: send \"What endpoints are available in that API?\"\n5. Turn 3: send \"Find documentation about the XYZ authentication protocol.\"\n6. `get_messages(session_id)` to capture trace\n7. Score and write JSON to `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\results\\rerun\\search_empty_fallback.json`\n\nScoring:\n- overall_score = correctness*0.25 + tool_selection*0.20 + context_retention*0.20 + completeness*0.15 + efficiency*0.10 + personality*0.05 + error_recovery*0.05\n- PASS if overall_score >= 6.0 AND no critical failure\n- T1 PASS: mentions \"Bearer token\" or \"Authorization header\" with source from api_reference.py\n- T2 PASS: mentions at least 2 of: /v1/chat/completions, /v1/models, /health\n- T3 PASS: says \"not found\" WITHOUT fabricating XYZ protocol details\n\n---\n\n## SCENARIO 2: smart_discovery\n**File:** `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\prompts\\run_smart_discovery.md`\n\nRead that prompt file for full instructions. Key facts:\n- Target file: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\corpus\\documents\\employee_handbook.md`\n- T1: \"What is the PTO policy for new employees?\" → 15 days (Section 4)\n- T2: \"What about the remote work policy?\" → up to 3 days per week with manager approval\n- Previous score: 2.75 FAIL\n- Fix applied: Agent session now persists cross-turn indexed documents (ui_session_id)\n- NO documents pre-indexed — agent must discover and index employee_handbook.md\n- Write result to: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\results\\rerun\\smart_discovery.json`\n\nSteps:\n1. `system_status()`\n2. `create_session(\"Eval: smart_discovery\")` — DO NOT call index_document\n3. Turn 1: send \"What is the PTO policy for new employees?\"\n   - CRITICAL FAIL if agent says \"no documents available\" without searching\n   - CRITICAL FAIL if agent answers without indexing a document\n   - PASS: agent discovers employee_handbook.md, indexes it, answers \"15 days\"\n4. Turn 2: send \"What about the remote work policy?\"\n   - PASS: agent uses already-indexed employee_handbook.md, answers \"3 days per week\"\n   - Deduct efficiency if agent re-indexes the same document\n5. `get_messages(session_id)`\n6. Score and write JSON\n\n---\n\n## SCENARIO 3: table_extraction\n**File:** `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\prompts\\run_table_extraction.md`\n\nRead that prompt file for full instructions. Key facts:\n- File: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\corpus\\documents\\sales_data_2025.csv`\n- T1: \"What was the best-selling product in March 2025 by revenue?\" → Widget Pro X ($28,400, 142 units)\n- T2: \"What was the total Q1 2025 revenue across all products?\" → $342,150\n- T3: \"Who was the top salesperson by total revenue in Q1?\" → Sarah Chen ($70,000)\n- Previous score: 4.08 FAIL (CRITICAL FAIL on T2 — agent claimed incomplete data was complete)\n- Fix applied: `analyze_data_file` now does fuzzy basename fallback to find file in indexed docs\n- Pre-index the CSV before sending messages (unlike smart_discovery)\n- CRITICAL FAIL: agent presents fabricated totals as \"complete\" without data-limitation caveat\n- Partial credit: if agent honestly says \"data may be incomplete\" that avoids CRITICAL FAIL\n- Write result to: `C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\results\\rerun\\table_extraction.json`\n\nSteps:\n1. `system_status()`\n2. `create_session(\"Eval: table_extraction\")`\n3. `index_document(session_id, \"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4\\eval\\corpus\\documents\\sales_data_2025.csv\")`\n   - Verify chunk_count > 0\n4. Turn 1: send \"What was the best-selling product in March 2025 by revenue?\"\n5. Turn 2: send \"What was the total Q1 2025 revenue across all products?\"\n6. Turn 3: send \"Who was the top salesperson by total revenue in Q1?\"\n7. `get_messages(session_id)`\n8. Score and write JSON\n\n---\n\n## Output JSON format (for each scenario)\n```json\n{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"...\",\n  \"run\": \"rerun_post_fix\",\n  \"previous_score\": 0.0,\n  \"status\": \"PASS or FAIL\",\n  \"overall_score\": 0.0,\n  \"turns\": [\n    {\n      \"turn\": 1,\n      \"user_message\": \"...\",\n      \"agent_response\": \"...\",\n      \"agent_tools\": [\"tool1\"],\n      \"scores\": {\"correctness\": 0, \"tool_selection\": 0, \"context_retention\": 0, \"completeness\": 0, \"efficiency\": 0, \"personality\": 0, \"error_recovery\": 0},\n      \"overall_score\": 0.0,\n      \"pass\": true,\n      \"failure_category\": null,\n      \"reasoning\": \"short explanation\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"root_cause\": null,\n  \"recommended_fix\": null,\n  \"improvement\": \"improved/regressed/no_change\",\n  \"fix_validated\": {\"fix_name\": true}\n}\n```\n\nRun all 3 scenarios sequentially. After all 3 are done, print a summary table:\n```\n| Scenario | Prev | New | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| search_empty_fallback | 5.40 | X.XX | PASS/FAIL |\n| smart_discovery | 2.75 | X.XX | PASS/FAIL |\n| table_extraction | 4.08 | X.XX | PASS/FAIL |\n```\n","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4","createdAt":"2026-03-20T11:12:02.956Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-20T11:39:23.862Z","sessionId":"3b27cb1e-4ca0-42ac-b51a-29172516e98d","systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Auto-title your task:**\n- Early in your work (after understanding the task), use `claudia_rename_task` to give YOUR OWN task a short, descriptive title (3-6 words) that reflects what you're actually doing\n- Your task ID is provided in the `claudia_rename_task` tool description — use it to rename yourself\n- If the user has manually edited your task title, the rename will be rejected — do NOT retry\n- If your work evolves significantly, update your title to reflect the new focus (unless user-edited)\n\n**Guidelines:**\n- Prefer 2-4 parallel tasks — don't over-decompose simple work\n- Only spawn tasks when parallelization provides real value; do simple work yourself\n- Each spawned task prompt should be fully self-contained — include file paths, context, and constraints so it can work independently\n- While waiting for spawned tasks, do NOT start implementing features that overlap with what they're doing\n- **NEVER delete or archive completed tasks** — the user wants to review their outputs. After a task completes, just report its status and read its output. Do NOT call `claudia_delete_task` or `claudia_archive_task` on finished tasks.","historySize":0,"displayName":"Eval Rerun: 3 FAIL Scenarios"},{"id":"task-1774006762715-1o04q4ics","prompt":"## Eval Re-Run: search_empty_fallback (rerun3)\n\n**Goal:** Re-run the `search_empty_fallback` eval scenario and record results in `eval/results/rerun/search_empty_fallback.json`. A code fix was applied since the last run — need to verify it pushes the score to ≥ 6.0 (PASS).\n\n**Code fix applied since rerun2 (already live in codebase):**\n- `file_tools.py` CWD search now skips `node_modules`, `.git`, `.venv`, `__pycache__`, etc. via `_SKIP_DIRS` set\n- This prevents `node_modules/api.md` from shadowing `eval/corpus/documents/api_reference.py`\n- `.py` extension was already added in the previous fix round\n\n**Scenario background:**\n- The agent must discover `api_reference.py` at `C:/Users/14255/Work/gaia4/eval/corpus/documents/api_reference.py`\n- The file documents a REST API with Bearer token authentication\n- In rerun2, agent found `node_modules/api.md` instead and gave wrong answers about EC key auth\n\n**Ground truth:**\n- T1: \"Bearer token via Authorization header\" (from api_reference.py)\n- T2: \"/v1/chat/completions, /v1/models, /health\" (endpoints from api_reference.py)\n- T3: \"XYZ protocol does NOT exist\" — agent should say not found, no fabrication\n\n**Scoring formula:**\n`score = correctness×0.25 + tool_selection×0.20 + context_retention×0.20 + completeness×0.15 + efficiency×0.10 + personality×0.05 + error_recovery×0.05`\nPASS = overall_score ≥ 6.0\n\n**Fix Protocol (use if agent fails):**\n- Fix 1: Re-send the original question exactly\n- Fix 2: \"Please check again — I believe the document has the answer.\"\n- Fix 3: Shorten/simplify the question\n- Fix 4: Re-state context from previous turns\n- Fix 5: \"Please check the document — I believe that figure may be incorrect.\"\nMax 2 fix attempts per turn before scoring as FAIL.\n\n**Steps:**\n1. Verify `_SKIP_DIRS` is present in `src/gaia/agents/tools/file_tools.py` (grep for `node_modules` in that file)\n2. Check that `api_reference.py` exists at `eval/corpus/documents/api_reference.py`\n3. Use `mcp__gaia-agent-ui__system_status` to verify the Agent UI server is running\n4. Create a new session: `mcp__gaia-agent-ui__create_session` with name \"search_empty_fallback_rerun3\"\n5. Run all 3 turns:\n\n**Turn 1:** Send: \"How does the API handle authentication? I think there's documentation somewhere.\"\n- Observe what files the agent finds and reads\n- Apply Fix Protocol if agent gives wrong answer (EC keys / wrong file)\n- Score all 7 dimensions\n\n**Turn 2:** Send: \"What endpoints are available in that API?\"\n- Agent should reference api_reference.py from T1\n- Score all 7 dimensions\n\n**Turn 3:** Send: \"Find documentation about the XYZ authentication protocol.\"\n- Agent should say \"not found\" — NO fabrication\n- Score all 7 dimensions\n\n6. Calculate overall_score = (T1_score + T2_score + T3_score) / 3\n\n7. Write results to `eval/results/rerun/search_empty_fallback.json`:\n```json\n{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"search_empty_fallback\",\n  \"run\": \"rerun3\",\n  \"session_id\": \"<actual session id>\",\n  \"previous_score\": 4.98,\n  \"status\": \"PASS or FAIL\",\n  \"overall_score\": <calculated>,\n  \"turns\": [...],\n  \"overall_score_calc\": \"...\",\n  \"improvement\": \"improved or regressed\",\n  \"root_cause\": \"...\",\n  \"recommended_fix\": \"...\",\n  \"notes\": \"...\",\n  \"cost_estimate\": {\"turns\": 3, \"fix_attempts\": <n>, \"estimated_usd\": 0.05}\n}\n```\n\n**Important:** Use only `mcp__gaia-agent-ui__*` tools for the Agent UI session. Do NOT call Python directly. The server must already be running (started by `gaia chat --ui`).\n\nAfter writing results, print a summary table:\n```\n| Scenario              | Prev  | New   | Delta | Status |\n| search_empty_fallback | 4.98  | X.XX  | +/-X  | ✅/❌  |\n```\n","workspaceId":"C:\\Users\\14255\\Work\\gaia4","createdAt":"2026-03-20T11:39:23.497Z","lastActivity":"2026-03-20T11:39:27.230Z","sessionId":null,"systemPrompt":"if it's a new feature, try to use a test cli unless it would be much easier to just have the user do a manual test (this is usually the case for visual features).. if it doesn't have functionality to do the test then add it. you can also use playwright mcp or curl if either of these would be easier. make sure you have enough logging to debug any issues.. if you create any test files, clean them up when you are done.  NEVER TOUCH PORT 4001.. if you are having issues with public apis, lookup examples online. always review your changes for gaps and issues after making extensive changes.\n\n\n## Claudia Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nYou are running as an agent inside Claudia, a multi-agent orchestrator. You have access to Claudia MCP tools (claudia_*) that let you collaborate with other agents.\n\n**IMPORTANT — Avoid duplicate work:**\n- Before starting any implementation, ALWAYS call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what other agents are already working on in this workspace\n- If another task is already handling a piece of work, do NOT implement it yourself — wait for that task to finish and read its output instead\n- After spawning tasks, your role shifts to **coordinator**: monitor, unblock, and integrate — do NOT start implementing the same work in parallel\n\n**When to spawn parallel tasks:**\n- When your work can be naturally decomposed into independent pieces (e.g., backend + frontend + tests)\n- When you need to research multiple topics simultaneously\n- When building a feature that has separable components\n\n**How to orchestrate:**\n1. Check existing tasks first — call `claudia_list_tasks` to see what's already running\n2. Plan — break remaining work into independent, parallelizable pieces\n3. Spawn — use `claudia_create_task` for each piece with a clear, self-contained prompt that includes all necessary context\n4. Wait and monitor — poll `claudia_get_task_status` periodically (every 30-60s) until tasks complete. Handle any that need input via `claudia_send_input`\n5. Review — use `claudia_get_task_output` to read results from completed tasks\n6. Integrate — review the combined changes for conflicts or integration issues, then fix any problems yourself\n\n**Task naming:**\n- When creating tasks, always provide a short `displayName` (e.g., \"Build API endpoint\", \"Write unit tests\") so tasks are easy to identify in the sidebar\n- Use `claudia_rename_task` to update your own task name if your work evolves beyond the original prompt\n\n**Auto-title your task:**\n- Early in your work (after understanding the task), use `claudia_rename_task` to give YOUR OWN task a short, descriptive title (3-6 words) that reflects what you're actually doing\n- Your task ID is provided in the `claudia_rename_task` tool 